      "content": "Swollen batteries, especially in a phone, are a serious fire hazard, so you must handle this with extreme caution. Do not try to puncture, squeeze, or otherwise manipulate the battery in any way. The immediate safety protocol is to isolate the device, remove the battery if it's easily accessible and safe to do so, and then dispose of it according to hazardous waste guidelines.\n\nFor the safest procedure, immediately take the phone and the swollen battery to a designated hazardous waste collection point or a reputable electronics recycling center. Do not throw it in regular trash, as this is a major fire risk. If you are in a shop environment, inform the technician immediately so they can follow proper safety protocols for lithium-ion battery disposal.",
